---
import { nurbling } from 'nurblings'
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro'

const REPO = 'https://github.com/albertesparragoza/nurblings'
---

<Site title="Nurbi and the brand" active="/brand/" class="brandp">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="brand-hero">
      <figure>
        <span class="av" set:html={nurbling('nurbi', { size: 300, title: 'Nurbi' })} />
        <figcaption>Nurbi, the flagship</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <h1>Every Nurbling is a relative of Nurbi.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Nurbi's two antennae are bezier control handles: the tools that turn an intention into a curve.
          Nurblings borrows the idea literally. Your handle becomes its handles.
        </p>
        <p class="lead">
          The family keeps Nurbi's soft lower body and plated crown, then stretches, widens and moves the plates
          around. Nurbi itself is never generated: a few reserved seeds show the original, and every other seed is
          kept a clear step away from it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rules">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Free to use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The library and every avatar it generates, in any project, commercial or not.</li>
          <li>Generated avatars are public domain under CC0: no attribution needed.</li>
          <li>Saying your project uses, or is built with, Nurblings.</li>
          <li>Forking the code under MIT, with a name of your own.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Ask first</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Publishing a fork, package or service under the Nurblings or Nurbi name.</li>
          <li>Using Nurbi as a mascot, logo or endorsement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The full terms are in <a href={`${REPO}/blob/develop/TRADEMARKS.md`}>TRADEMARKS.md</a>. Unsure?
          <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>Open an issue</a> and ask.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Site>

<style is:global>
  .brandp .brand-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(40px, 7vw, 88px);
  }

  .brandp figure {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    background: var(--tint);
    border-radius: var(--r-xl);
    padding: 32px;
  }

  .brandp figcaption {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .brandp h1 {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  .brandp .rules {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .brandp .rules h2 {
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .brandp .rules ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .brandp .rules a {
    color: var(--accent-text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .brandp .brand-hero,
    .brandp .rules {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
